<title>PERU: Peru's net int'l reserves rise to $9.571 billion.</title>
<headline>Peru's net int'l reserves rise to $9.571 billion.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Monday its net international reserves rose to $9.571 billion by May 28, up from $9.541 billion the week before.</p>
<p>Peru's reserves, which have recovered steadily since President Alberto Fujimori's government took power in 1990, ended last year at $8.540 billion.</p>
<p>The government estimates reserves will rise above $10 billion by mid-1998.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima Newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
